\description{
Read a label-free experimental design out of an SDRF, in MetaMorpheus's terms, or every reason it was refused.

Calls mzLib's \code{SdrfLabelFreeDesign.Read}. It runs every check MetaMorpheus's own design validator
runs and \strong{refuses rather than repairs}: a factor written \code{not available}, two files claiming the
same replicate and fraction, a document with several factor columns and no declaration - each is
a refusal, and all of them are reported at once. It relabels in only two ways, both recorded in
\code{notes}: study-wide biological replicate numbers are ranked within each condition (\code{22 -> 1}),
and rows for files the search does not read are dropped.
}
\details{
\strong{A refusal is an answer, not an error.} When \code{is_valid} is \code{FALSE}, \code{refusals} lists every
reason and \code{records} has no rows, so a design MetaMorpheus would reject cannot be used by
mistake. mzLib refuses because MetaMorpheus skips quantification with only a warning when its
design file is invalid.
}
\value{
An \code{mzlibr_sdrf_design}: \code{path}; \code{is_valid}; \code{file_key_column}, the column runs were keyed
  on (\code{NA} when the SDRF names no file, itself a refusal); \code{condition_columns} used, in join
  order; \code{condition_columns_declared} and \code{searched_files_given}; \code{file_count} files (runs) in the
  design, 0 when refused; \code{refusals} and \code{notes} in mzLib's words; \code{report}, mzLib's account of
  all of it; \code{written} (\code{path}, \code{file_count}), or \code{NULL}; \code{caveats}; and \code{records}, one row per
  run in SDRF row order: \code{full_path}, \code{file_name} (the run key, \code{Intensity_<file_name>}),
  \code{condition}, and \code{biological_replicate}, \code{technical_replicate} and \code{fraction}, \strong{0-based}, as
  the quant functions take them. \code{ExperimentalDesign.tsv} writes the same numbers plus one.

}
\section{From SDRF to FlashLFQ}{


\code{\link{sdrf_design_spectra}} gives the design as \code{\link{flashlfq_quantify}} takes \code{spectra}, and
\code{\link{sdrf_design_run_design}} as \code{\link{flashlfq_median_polish}} takes \code{design}, so the SDRF drives the
quantification with no hand-written design. Both refuse a refused design.

Label-free only: an isobaric (TMT, iTRAQ) SDRF needs a channel design this does not produce. See
\code{\link{isobaric_kits}} for the channels themselves.

}
