\section{Parameters: units, ranges and defaults}{
\describe{
\item{\code{path}}{path; required. One .sdrf.tsv file. A file that does not exist is a usage error.}
\item{\code{condition_columns} (wire \code{--condition-columns})}{string; default absent. The factor value[...] columns the condition is built from, by exact (case-sensitive) name, separated by TAB characters, in join order; the condition is their values joined with "_". Absent: mzLib uses the document's only factor column, and refuses a document with several. Given but blank, or with a blank name, is a usage error.}
\item{\code{searched_files} (wire \code{--searched-files-stdin})}{flag; default absent. stdin holds the files the search will read, one per line, as paths or bare names. Each must be named EXACTLY (case and extension) by one row; rows for other files are dropped and reported in notes; the searched paths replace the SDRF's names in full_path. An empty list is mzLib's refusal, not a usage error.}
\item{\code{out}}{path; default absent. Also write MetaMorpheus's ExperimentalDesign.tsv (1-based) here, through mzLib's writer. Must end in .tsv, case-insensitive (PYB-1), checked before the SDRF is read. Written only when is_valid; a refused design writes nothing and written is null.}
}
}
\section{Returned fields}{
Each field with its type, its unit, and what \code{NA} means when it is \code{NA}.

\describe{
\item{\code{path}}{string; never \code{NA}. The SDRF path as given.}
\item{\code{is_valid}}{bool; never \code{NA}. No refusals. False is an answer, not an error: the table is then empty.}
\item{\code{file_key_column}}{string; \code{NA} when the SDRF has neither comment[searched data file] nor comment[data file], so no row names a file (also a refusal). The column files were keyed on: comment[searched data file] when present, else comment[data file] (mapping row MAP-12).}
\item{\code{condition_columns}}{string[]; never \code{NA}. The factor columns the condition was built from, in join order; empty when none could be chosen.}
\item{\code{condition_columns_declared}}{bool; never \code{NA}. Whether \code{--condition-columns} was given.}
\item{\code{searched_files_given}}{bool; never \code{NA}. Whether \code{--searched-files-stdin} was given.}
\item{\code{file_count}}{int; in \strong{files}; never \code{NA}. Rows in the table; 0 when refused.}
\item{\code{refusals}}{string[]; never \code{NA}. Every reason the design was refused, all at once, in mzLib's words. Empty when valid.}
\item{\code{notes}}{string[]; never \code{NA}. Every relabelling on the way to a valid design: biological replicates ranked within a condition, with the old -> new mapping (MAP-33), and rows dropped because the search does not read their file.}
\item{\code{report}}{string; never \code{NA}. mzLib's human-readable account (SdrfLabelFreeDesign.Report): counts, key column, condition columns, notes, refusals.}
\item{\code{column_names}}{string[]; never \code{NA}. The table's columns in order.}
\item{\code{records} (wire \code{columns})}{table; never \code{NA}. Column name to one value per file, in SDRF row order.}
\item{\code{written}}{object; \code{NA} when \code{--out} was not given, or the design was refused and nothing was written. \{path, file_count\} of the ExperimentalDesign.tsv written.}
\item{\code{caveats}}{string[]; never \code{NA}. Six static caveats.}
}
}
\section{Columns of \code{records}}{
\describe{
\item{\code{full_path}}{string; never \code{NA}. The file as the SDRF's key column names it, or the matching searched path when \code{--searched-files-stdin} was given.}
\item{\code{file_name}}{string; never \code{NA}. full_path's file name without its extension (SpectraFileInfo.FilenameWithoutExtension): the run key the quant verbs use.}
\item{\code{condition}}{string; never \code{NA}. The condition columns' values joined with _.}
\item{\code{biological_replicate}}{int; never \code{NA}. 0-based, ranked within the condition (ExperimentalDesign.tsv's Biorep minus 1).}
\item{\code{technical_replicate}}{int; never \code{NA}. 0-based (Techrep minus 1).}
\item{\code{fraction}}{int; never \code{NA}. 0-based (Fraction minus 1).}
}
}
\section{Errors}{
Each is an R condition carrying the class shown and \code{mzlib_error}; see \code{\link{mzlib_error}}.

\describe{
\item{\code{mzlib_usage_error} (usage)}{path missing or the file does not exist}
\item{\code{mzlib_usage_error} (usage)}{\code{--out} without a value, or not ending in .tsv (checked before the SDRF is read)}
\item{\code{mzlib_usage_error} (usage)}{\code{--condition-columns} without a value, or with a blank name}
\item{\code{mzlib_bridge_error} (correctness)}{mzLib cannot parse the SDRF at all, or the \code{--out} directory cannot be written}
\item{\code{mzlib_service_unavailable} (service_unavailable)}{Never raised by this verb.}
}
}
\section{Caveats}{
\itemize{
\item Label-free only. An isobaric (TMT, iTRAQ) SDRF needs a channel design this verb does not produce.
\item is_valid = false is an answer: refusals lists every reason at once and the table is empty. mzLib refuses rather than repairs because MetaMorpheus skips quantification with only a warning when its design file is invalid.
\item The table is 0-based, as SpectraFileInfo and the quant verbs take it. ExperimentalDesign.tsv is 1-based; mzLib converts when it writes.
\item notes is the only record of a renumbering; read it.
\item A factor holding not available or not applicable is refused: it would pair samples nobody said were alike.
\item MetaMorpheus finds the design only as a file named ExperimentalDesign.tsv beside the spectra; \code{--out} writes any .tsv path.
}
}
\section{Performance}{
Every call starts one bridge process, which costs a .NET start-up before any work. 
